Analyzer -- the class of all lexical analyzers
**********************************************

Description
===========

A function that accepts input in its original form and separates it into
tokens, will be called a *note lexical analyzer: Analyzer,. These analyzers are
functional: call one with the original input, and it returns a function of 0
arguments (with changeable internal state) that keeps returning tokens each
time it is called until none are left. Actually, the analyzer is to return a
pair: (pos,token), where pos is a string indicating the position where token
was found in the input. A position will be a sort of thing which can be
converted to string with *note toString: (Macaulay2Doc)toString, (for printing
error messages) and can be sorted.

* Menu:

* charAnalyzer::                a lexical analyzer that provides characters from a string one at a time
* nonspaceAnalyzer::            a lexical analyzer that provides non-white-space characters from a string one at a time

Methods that use a lexical analyzer:
====================================

  * *note Parser _colon_ Analyzer: Parser _co Analyzer, -- combine a parser
    with a lexical analyzer to make a complete system

Protected objects of class Analyzer:
====================================

  * *note charAnalyzer: charAnalyzer, -- a lexical analyzer that provides
    characters from a string one at a time
  * *note nonspaceAnalyzer: nonspaceAnalyzer, -- a lexical analyzer that
    provides non-white-space characters from a string one at a time

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Analyzer: Analyzer, is a *note self initializing type:
