optP -- making a parser optional
********************************

  * Usage: 
        optP p
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note parser: Parser,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note parser: Parser,, a parser that accepts tokens accepted by p and
        returns the value returned by p, or accepts the empty sequence of
        tokens and returns the symbol nil.  It prefers to do the former.

Description
===========

After the first token, the parser is no slower than p would have been.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (optP constParser "abc" : charAnalyzer) "abc"|
|                                                  |
|o1 = abc                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (optP constParser "abc" : charAnalyzer) ""   |
|                                                  |
|o2 = nil                                          |
|                                                  |
|o2 : Symbol                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------+

