andP -- parser conjunction
**************************

  * Usage: 
        r = andP(p,q,...)
  * Inputs:
      * (p,q,...), a sequence of parsers (of type *note Parser: Parser,)
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note parser: Parser,, a parser that accepts as many tokens as p
        will accept, then as many as q will accept, and so on.  The return
        value is the sequence of values returned by each of the input parsers.

Description
===========

An abbreviation for andP(p,q) is p@q.

If one of the arguments is a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, then *note
constParser: constParser, is used to convert it into a parser.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (constParser "abc" @ constParser "def" : charAnalyzer) "abcdef"|
|                                                                    |
|o1 = (abc, def)                                                     |
|                                                                    |
|o1 : Sequence                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

